<article class="env-definition" id="03YP">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03YP">Definition <span data-tag="03YP">94.12.3</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme contained in $\mathit{Sch}_{fppf}$. The <em>$2$-category of algebraic stacks over $S$</em> is the sub $2$-category of the $2$-category of categories fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ (see Categories, Definition <a href="/tag/02XS" data-tag="02XS">4.35.6</a>) defined as follows: </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
Its objects are those categories fibred in groupoids over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$ which are algebraic stacks over $S$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Its $1$-morphisms $f : \mathcal{X} \to \mathcal{Y}$ are any functors of categories over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$, as in Categories, Definition <a href="/tag/003Y" data-tag="003Y">4.32.1</a>. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
Its $2$-morphisms are transformations between functors over $(\mathit{Sch}/S)_{fppf}$, as in Categories, Definition <a href="/tag/003Y" data-tag="003Y">4.32.1</a>. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>